## 7. Live Coding Compiler

### 7.1 Permitted Use

The in-browser compiler is provided as an educational tool. You may use it to write, test, and run code for personal learning and experimentation.

### 7.2 Prohibited Use

You must not use the compiler to:

- Write, execute, or distribute malicious code, including viruses, worms, trojans, or exploits
- Perform denial-of-service attacks or attempt to overwhelm any server or network
- Mine cryptocurrency
- Access or probe external systems without authorization
- Circumvent usage limits through automated or scripted requests

### 7.3 Usage Limits

Compiler usage may be subject to rate limits, execution time caps, or resource constraints depending on your plan. We reserve the right to throttle or suspend compiler access if we detect abusive usage patterns.

### 7.4 No Persistence Guarantee

Code saved in the compiler is provided as a convenience. We do not guarantee the indefinite storage of your compiler sessions or saved files. You are responsible for maintaining your own backups of important code.

